  "details": "- Rebase onto the vendor's 2.4.62-13.9 source package\n- Nine TuxCare duplicates are dropped; the vendor now ships its own patches of\n  the same upstream commits, covering mod_auth_digest nonce-count tracking and\n  one-time nonce enforcement, the mod_charset_lite heap buffer overflow, the\n  mod_heartmonitor NULL pointer dereference, the mod_proxy_ftp PASV reply\n  address check, oversized Host header handling in mod_vhost_alias, the\n  mod_rewrite lookahead denial of service, the mod_xml2enc charset conversion\n  failure, the mod_dav_fs property database integer overflow and crafted\n  Transfer-Encoding responses in mod_proxy_uwsgi\n- Retained TuxCare fixes that the vendor does not ship: mod_headers.c trusted\n  Content-Type handling, reason-phrase control character rejection in\n  http_filters.c and server/protocol.c, mod_proxy_ftp.c directory listing\n  escaping, shared lock limiting in modules/dav/main/util.c, .DAV state\n  directory access denial in modules/dav/fs/repos.c, the SSLRequire\n  file()/filesize() restriction in ssl_engine_config.c, mod_userdir.c \".\" user\n  name rejection, and mod_session_cookie.c session cookie removal",
